# Cloudflare response headers.
# Image and font filenames end in a content code (e.g. -7fdd711), so a changed file gets a new name
# and browsers can keep the old one for a year. Give any new image or font a new name when it changes.
# CSS and JS keep fixed names, so they use Cloudflare's default (recheck on each visit).
# Security headers apply to every page. The application form posts to Google Apps Script, which answers
# from script.googleusercontent.com, so both are allowed in connect-src. Cloudflare Web Analytics injects its
# beacon from static.cloudflareinsights.com and reports to cloudflareinsights.com. Inline styles hold image focal points.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://script.google.com https://script.googleusercontent.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

/assets/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
